Z||000000||FieroMike||08-17-2000||01:57 PM||||Hi guys! I need some feedback on which car I should pick up.  These are the contenders:<P>'85 GT v-6 Auto<BR>lower 100K miles<BR>new windshield/brakes<BR>black-decent paint<BR>interior is nice<BR>power everything<P>'86 SE v-6 Auto<BR>65K miles<BR>black-decent paint<BR>interior is nice<BR>power everything<P>The '85 is $1,350 and the '86 is $900.  I am looking for a car to fix up to immaculate condition.  Which one is faster stock vs stock??  I will be changing out the Auto to a manual either way.  The SE has a rear spoiler.  What do you guys think??? I need your help here!!<P>Thanks<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||86SE||08-17-2000||02:36 PM||||Excellent find!  I would deffinently buy the 86SE.<P>Because:<BR>1)  The 86SE looks exactly like an 85GT.<BR>2) Extremely low miles, considering the year.<BR>3) The price!<P>Stock for stock, I would say they are equaly fast.<P>Join us 86SE people!  <P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Stering wheel<BR>Gas AND brake petals<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||10
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||08-17-2000||02:40 PM||||<BR>At those prices, buy both.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
